#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Idempotence.** Running `B` twice over `R` produces a target state equal to running it once (compare per-slice content hashes)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Determinism.** Running `B` with the same inputs and logic version on two occasions produces identical outputs (per-slice hash equality)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Scope.** `B` modifies no row outside `R` (snapshot diff of the commit touches only files/rows in `R`; per-slice hashes outside `R` unchanged)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Completeness.** For every slice in `R`: `count(source) = count(target) + count(quarantine) + count(explicitly excluded)`."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Accuracy.** For every slice in `R`, control totals of additive measures and the aggregate row hash over canonicalised business columns match between source and target, or every mismatch is listed and explained."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**No regression of freshness.** For every key, the target's source version after `B` is ≥ its version before `B`."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Attribution.** Every row in `R` carries the logic version and run id that produced it, and `count(rows in R with logic_version ≠ target) = 0` when `B` completes."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Provenance.** Every row loaded from another system carries its source system, source key and extract identifier; none is null."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Atomic visibility.** Consumers observe either the pre-`B` or the post-`B` state of each published unit (slice, table, or table set), never a partial one (published via overwrite commit, branch fast-forward or view swap)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Reversibility.** The pre-`B` state is recoverable for a declared window (snapshot id, tag, retained old table, or branch), and the restore procedure has been exercised."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Source protection.** During `B`, source latency and replication lag stay within declared thresholds; `B` paused automatically when they did not."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Ordering.** For each table, every dimension (and reference table) that `R`'s facts reference was complete for `R` before the facts were loaded; type 2 dimensions were processed in event-time order."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Time zone.** Per-day counts in source and target agree when both are bucketed in UTC."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**Restatement record.** If `B` changed any previously published value, the restatement log has an entry with slices, reason, old and new totals, and logic versions."
msgstr ""

#: docs/guides/backfill.md
msgid "**PII.** Every personal-data column in the target is on the approved inventory with its treatment; quarantine and landing copies follow the same retention."
msgstr ""

